            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for a newspaper, then the Telugu for a number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: పెళ్ళికూతురు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పెళ్ళికూతురు — peḷḷikūturu — \"a bride\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "పెళ్ళికూతురు (peḷḷikūturu) is native Dravidian: peḷḷi, \"marriage\" (DEDR 4395), and a nasalised kūturu, \"daughter\", which DEDR 1873 lists with Kannada kūsu, \"infant; maiden\": \"the wedding daughter\". DEDR compares Sanskrit kūkuda, \"one who gives a girl in marriage\", a lexicon word, with the second."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for this chapter."
            }
          ]
        },
